// GPUI's drawing model in Coax, for the Zeron-fork UI (docs/desktop/coax-desktop.md).
// GPUI (zeronsh/zui, the renderer Zeron draws with) paints a frame as
// primitives: quads (a rounded rect with a fill and a border), drop shadows
// (a gaussian-blurred rounded rect) and monochrome sprites (glyphs and SVG
// icons, alpha masks in an atlas, tinted). These are the same three, written
// as vertices for apps/openagents-desktop/Zeron.metal, which ports GPUI's
// fragment shaders. Layout is in logical pixels; a primitive's bounds snap to
// device pixels the way GPUI's window.rs does (snap_bounds, cover_bounds).
// Two more for the transcript: the activity rail's elbow (paint_elbow, a
// quadratic bend into a straight branch, as transcript.rs paints it with a
// path) and Zeron's EdgeFade, a per-vertex fade band at the top and bottom
// of the transcript (gp_fade, floats 24..27 of a vertex). And two for
// Zeron's glass (glass.rs Plate): a vertical gradient fill (GPUI's
// linear_gradient at 180 degrees) and an inset shadow without blur, the
// lit top edge (paint_inset_shadows). An attachment chip in a line of text
// is one code point in Supplementary Private Use Area-A (GP_CHIP_BASE + its
// number): it measures and paints as Zeron's chip (composer/chip.rs), its
// label padded with no-break spaces over a pill with the icon's well.
//
// The host is GPUI's platform layer: it rasterizes Zeron's font (Geist) with
// CoreText exactly as gpui_macos/text_system.rs does (four subpixel x
// positions, the font-smoothing dilation picked from the text's luminance)
// and Zeron's SVG icons at twice their device size, into one atlas, and
// gives Coax each font's metrics and each icon's tile (gp_font_*, gp_icon).
// Based on Zeron by Wing, MIT.
//
// This file is now only the way in: the code moved into the component
// system's layers (components/spec.md, GitHub #13153). Colours and text are
// core/color.coax and core/text.coax; the fonts' metrics, the glyph cache
// and measuring are layout/font.coax; rounding is layout/round.coax; the
// vertices are backend/gpu.coax. The names are the same.

#load "../backend/gpu.coax";
